														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4623933">
									

<p>This doesn't <em>quite</em> hit it with me. I really appreciate the details given with the initial discovery and the following interview log. That kind of misfortune and display of police corruption really makes me feel for Father Pedro, especially since he gives into his community. This kind of unfairness is tangible and sticks well.</p>
<p>However, I think the issue I have with this lies in the latter half. There's a little bit of struggle with the conpoc revision proposal, but to have the item be given up with so little resistance makes it seem&#8230; trivial, I guess. If it was just a case of pitching the proposal to the site director, it's a wonder that Dizon didn't do that sooner.</p>
<p>I think I would have personally preferred a bigger &quot;fight for what's right&quot; here. While I can get behind a Foundation that does something obviously good for once, this feels as if it resolves itself almost too easily.</p>

							</div>

								
					
